ssing-the-bridge noodles","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Yunnan cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Crossing-the-bridge noodles is a rice noodle soup that originates from Yunnan province of China. It is one of the best-known dishes in Yunnan cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-crossing-the-bridge-noodles"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crossing-the-bridge_noodles"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Yunnan cuisine","cuisine/yunnan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"China South of the Clouds","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"chinasouthoftheclouds.com","note":"Yunnan recipes, ingredient guides and travel notes tied to Georgia Freedman's Yunnan cookbook.","url":"https://chinasouthoftheclouds.com/category/recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/92/Crossing_the_Bridge_Noodle_at_Qian_Xiang_Yuan.jpg/500px-Crossing_the_Bridge_Noodle_at_Qian_Xiang_Yuan.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Baycrest","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.5","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.5","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Crossing_the_Bridge_Noodle_at_Qian_Xiang_Yuan.jpg"}},"ingredient/raspberries":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/raspberries","n":"Raspberries","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["The raspberry is the edible fruit of several plant species in the genus Rubus of the rose family, most of which are in the subgenus Idaeobatus, and these plants themselves. Raspberries are perennial with woody stems."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-raspberries"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberries"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Jammie Dodgers","dish/jammie-dodgers"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Raspberries","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":945254,"top":[["Russia","cuisine/russian-cuisine",205292],["Mexico","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",171329],["Serbia","cuisine/serbian-cuisine",107611],["Poland","cuisine/polish-cuisine",101000],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",78548],["Morocco","cuisine/moroccan-cuisine",51388],["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",41438],["Ukraine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine",34462],["Portugal","cuisine/portuguese-cuisine",30321],["United Kingdom","cuisine/british-cuisine",15964],["Bosnia and Herz.","cuisine/bosnian-cuisine",14501],["Chile","cuisine/chilean-cuisine",13471],["Azerbaijan","cuisine/azerbaijani-cuisine",11795],["Kazakhstan","cuisine/kazakh-cuisine",10916],["Germany","cuisine/german-cuisine",6912]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Apples","ingredient/apples"],["Malic acid","ingredient/malic-acid"],["Raspberry jam","ingredient/raspberry-jam"],["Shortbread","ingredient/shortbread"],["Sodium bicarbonate","ingredient/sodium-bicarbonate"],["Strawberries","ingredient/strawberries"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tartaric acid","ingredient/tartaric-acid"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/2b/Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/500px-Raspberries_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Ivar Leidus","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raspberries_(Rubus_idaeus).jpg"}},"dish/karelian-hot-pot":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/karelian-hot-pot","n":"Karelian hot pot","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Finnish cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The Karelian hot pot (British) or Karelian stew (US) (Karelian: päččiliha Karelian pronunciation: [ˈpæt.t͜ɕiˌlʲiɦɑ̝]; Finnish: karjalanpaisti) is a traditional Finnish meat stew originating in the region of Karelia. It is commonly prepared using a combination of pork and beef, but elk or lamb can also be used. Along with the Karelian pasties (šipainiekat, karjalanpiirakat), it is the most widely recognized Karelian food in Finland. In 2007, it was selected as the national dish of Finland by the readers of the Finnish tabloid Iltalehti. In a similar poll organized by the ELO Foundation for the Promotion of Finnish Food Culture in cooperation with the Central Union of Agricultural Producers and Forest Owners (MTK) and the Finnish Ministry of Agriculture and Forestry in autumn 2016, Karelian hot pot took second place, losing to rye bread."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-karelian-hot-pot"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karelian_hot_pot"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Finnish cuisine","cuisine/finnish-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Black pepper","ingredient/black-pepper"],["Lamb","ingredient/lamb"],["Pork","ingredient/pork"]]},{"h":"More from Finnish cuisine","links":[["Blodpalt","dish/blodpalt"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Egg butter","dish/egg-butter"],["Glögg","dish/glogg"],["Joulutorttu","dish/joulutorttu"],["Kalakukko","dish/kalakukko"],["Kesäkeitto","dish/kesakeitto"],["Kringle","dish/kringle"],["Kuivaliha","dish/kuivaliha"],["Lanttulaatikko","dish/lanttulaatikko"],["Lohikeitto","dish/lohikeitto"],["Lörtsy","dish/lortsy"],["Semla","dish/semla"],["Smörgåstårta","dish/smorgastarta"],["Strong beer","dish/strong-beer"]]}]},"dish/kue-satu":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kue-satu","n":"Kue satu","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Kue satu (in West Java and Jakarta) or kue koya (in Central and East Java) is a popular traditional kue kering (dry traditional cookie) made of sweet white-colored mung bean powder that crumbles when bitten. It is commonly found as a traditional cookie in Indonesia, especially in Java. In Indonesia, this cookie is often served during festive occasions, such as Lebaran (Eid al Fitr), Natal (Christmas), and Imlek (Chinese new year). It is believed that the cookies were derived from Chinese Peranakan traditional cookies or dry kue."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kue-satu"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kue_satu"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Mung bean","ingredient/mung-bean"],["Mung beans","ingredient/mung-beans"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Vanilla","ingredient/vanilla"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/1b/Kue_satu_2.JPG/500px-Kue_satu_2.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Midori","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kue_satu_2.JPG"}},"dish/lasagna":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/lasagna","n":"Lasagna","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Italian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Lasagna, also known by the plural form lasagne, is a type of pasta made in wide, flat sheets.  It originates in Italian cuisine, where it is served in a number of ways, but is most often served as a casserole made by stacked layers of pasta, alternating with fillings that could consist of meat, dairy, vegetables, and sauces. Typically, cooked pasta is assembled with the aforementioned fillings, topped with grated cheese, and then baked in an oven (al forno). Regional variations of this are found across Italy, along with Americanized versions worldwide."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-lasagna"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lasagna"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Italian cuisine","cuisine/italian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Béchamel sauce","ingredient/bechamel-sauce"],["Parmesan","ingredient/parmesan"],["Ragù","ingredient/ragu"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pasta Grannies","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pastagrannies.substack.com","note":"Vicky Bennison's long-running video series filming Italian grandmothers making regional pasta by hand.","url":"https://pastagrannies.substack.com/p/pasta-grannies-is-now-on-substack","suggested":true,"kind":"youtube"},{"name":"Recipes from Italy","color":