o","dish/pecorino"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/06/Meaty_Lasagna_8of8_%288736299782%29.jpg/500px-Meaty_Lasagna_8of8_%288736299782%29.jpg","w":500,"h":321,"by":"Breville USA","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meaty_Lasagna_8of8_(8736299782).jpg"}},"ingredient/swiss-cheese-north-america":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/swiss-cheese-north-america","n":"Swiss cheese (North America)","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["The term \"Swiss cheese\" is used for any variety of cheese that resembles Emmental cheese, a yellow, medium-hard cheese that originated in the area around Emmental, Switzerland. It is classified as a Swiss-type or Alpine cheese. The term is generic; it does not imply that the cheese is actually made in Switzerland. Some types of Swiss cheese have a distinctive appearance, as the blocks or rounds of the cheese are riddled with holes known as \"eyes\". Cheese without eyes is known as \"blind\"."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-swiss-cheese-north-america"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swiss_cheese_(North_America)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Reuben sandwich","dish/reuben-sandwich"]]],["Jewish cuisine","cuisine/jewish-cuisine",[["Reuben sandwich","dish/reuben-sandwich"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Corned beef","ingredient/corned-beef"],["Russian dressing","ingredient/russian-dressing"],["Rye bread","ingredient/rye-bread"],["Sauerkraut","ingredient/sauerkraut"],["Thousand Island dressing","ingredient/thousand-island-dressing"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ec/NCI_swiss_cheese.jpg/500px-NCI_swiss_cheese.jpg","w":500,"h":545,"by":"Renee Comet (photographer)","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NCI_swiss_cheese.jpg"}},"ingredient/breadfruit":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/breadfruit","n":"Breadfruit","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 0 dishes across 0 cuisines","intro":[["ʻUlu is a starchy, high-yield fruit that grows in the upland forest zone in ",["Kānaka Maoli foodways","cuisine/kanaka-maoli-foodways"],". Hawaiian growers are working to plant far more of it."]],"src":"note","sources":[{"name":"National Museum of the American Indian, American Indian magazine, The breath of life","url":"https://www.americanindianmagazine.org/story/the-breath-of-life"}],"actions":[{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Breadfruit"}],"sections":[{"h":"Mentioned in","links":[["Kānaka Maoli foodways","cuisine/kanaka-maoli-foodways"]]}]}}